  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 115 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nSaturday through Wednesday:\n\nLow pressure continues northeast across Ontario Canada on\nSaturday, dragging a cold front into the midwest. Breezy south\nto southwest winds and warm weather (highs in the low to mid\n60s) continue Saturday, followed by a period of rain showers (60-85%\nchances) ahead of and along the cold front Saturday evening into\nSunday morning. Models have come into much better agreement on\nthe arrival time of the cold front; our best guess is for \nnorthwest winds to arrive around dawn Sunday morning. As such, \nour Sunday high temp forecast calls for upper 40s to mid 50s \n(warmest towards southeastern WI) as CAA kicks in. Some 15-50%\nprecip chances taper off into Sunday afternoon as the cooler /\ndrier airmass arrives. \n\nFrom Monday through midweek next week, expecting daytime highs \nin the upper 30s to low 40s, with lows in the low to mid 20s \n(locally warmer by Lake MI). Predominantly dry weather expected \nthrough this period as high pressure settles into the Great \nLakes region. \n\nSheppard",
